course: dictionary
lesson: 7088
title: Payment
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A payment is money that is paid for something. «Payment by card» means paying with a card instead of cash. Payment can also mean the act of paying, so the word covers both the money and the action.
explain: Use the words around it to check the meaning. «Real police do not ask for payment by message or phone.» The sentence shows that a payment is money someone is asked to send, so a stranger asking for one is a warning sign.
explain: Payments can also repeat. «A mortgage is a huge loan from a bank to buy a home, paid back monthly.» Those monthly payments come again and again until the loan is paid off, and if they stop, the bank can take the home back.
fact: A payment is money that is paid for something.
fact: «Payment» can mean the act of paying, as in «payment by card».
fact: Payments are often the same amount each week or month, like rent and bills.
fact: A «down payment» is a first payment that can be a different amount from the rest.
fact: Never give payment details to strangers online, and remember that real police do not ask for payment by message or phone.
exercise: «The shop asked for payment in cash.» What does payment mean here? | A kind of bag for shopping | A list of the things in the shop | *Money paid for something | A long walk home
exercise: «Missing payments lowers a credit score.» What does missing payments mean? | Paying more than you need to | Counting the money twice | Paying with a card | *Not paying when you should
exercise: A message says, «Pay or be arrested.» Why is this a warning sign? | *Real police do not ask for payment by message or phone | Police always send messages like this | It is a friendly offer of help | Payment is always free
test: «Ransomware is criminal software that locks files and demands payment.» What does demands payment mean? | Makes the files bigger | Forgets the files | *Asks for money to be paid | Sends a birthday card
test: «A mortgage is a huge loan from a bank to buy a home.» What is a mortgage? | A small gift from a friend | *A huge loan from a bank to buy a home | A type of card for shops | A cheap bus ticket
exam: A message asks you for a payment and a gift card code; what should you do? | *Ignore it and tell an adult | Reply with your password to check it | Send the gift card code straight away | Click the link quickly before it expires
